<title>USA: Iomega Corp Q2 net income up 85.7pct.</title>
<headline>Iomega Corp Q2 net income up 85.7pct.</headline>
<dateline>ROY, Utah 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iomega Corp.</p>
<p>		 (In thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>		    For the Three Months Ended</p>
<p>						   Jun 29,     Jun 30,</p>
<p>						     1997	   1996</p>
<p> Sales					  $400,162    $283,638</p>
<p> Gross margin				  117,459	76,195</p>
<p> Net income				     26,209	14,082</p>
<p> Net income per common share		  0.19	  0.11</p>
<p> Weighted average shares outstanding   136,452     132,405</p>
<p>			 For the Six Months Ended</p>
<p>						   Jun 29,     Jun 30,</p>
<p>							1997	 1996</p>
<p> Sales					  $761,506    $505,626</p>
<p> Gross margin				  224,738     136,095</p>
<p> Net income				     49,223	24,203</p>
<p> Net income per common share		  0.36	  0.19</p>
<p> Weighted average shares outstanding   136,078     130,419</p>
<p>NOTE: -- Iomega says excluding the expenses associated with the recall of approximately 75,000 Jaz (R) cartridges, which was announced on April 25, 1997, Iomega's earnings would have been 21 cents per share for Q2.</p>
</text>
